Interpolation cases with one class per block. The same `cases.re` and
`other.re` build as a native executable (server-reason-react) and as a
Melange library; both must give the same classes and variable names.

  $ cat > dune-project << EOF
  > (lang dune 3.10)
  > (using melange 0.1)
  > EOF

  $ cat > native/dune << EOF
  > (executable
  >  (name main)
  >  (libraries
  >   server-reason-react.js
  >   server-reason-react.belt
  >   server-reason-react.react
  >   server-reason-react.reactDom
  >   styled-ppx.native)
  >  (preprocess
  >   (pps styled-ppx --native server-reason-react.ppx server-reason-react.melange_ppx)))
  > EOF

  $ cat > js/dune << EOF
  > (copy_files ../native/{cases,other}.re)
  > (library
  >  (name cases_js)
  >  (modes melange)
  >  (libraries styled-ppx.melange reason-react)
  >  (preprocess
  >   (pps styled-ppx reason-react-ppx melange.ppx)))
  > (melange.emit
  >  (target out)
  >  (modules)
  >  (libraries cases_js))
  > EOF

  $ dune build

Native markup. Each element carries its own values in `style`. A merge
lists both pairs. Each block has its own variables: one block used twice
(`f`) repeats one variable and the later value wins; two different blocks
(`a1` and `b1`, `Cases.a1` and `Other.a1`) set different variables and the
sheet order decides.

